{"step_index":72,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-02T21:44:37Z","content":"# Law Enforcement Intelligence Platform — FastAPI Backend\n\nThis is a complete, standalone, production-ready FastAPI backend application engineered for a law enforcement intelligence platform. It features:\n- **CORS Middleware** configured for secure frontend integrations (Vite/React).\n- **Neo4j Database Session Dependency** with lifecycle management and connection pooling.\n- **Header-Based RBAC Enforcement** (`X-Auth-Token`) restricting access to personnel with the `investigator` role.\n- **Graph Topology Serialization** converting Neo4j Cypher results (`MATCH (n) OPTIONAL MATCH (n)-[r]->(m)`) into the exact Cytoscape.js elements specification (`id`, `source`, `target`, `label`).\n- **Automated Anomaly Detection Engine Mock** returning prioritized syndication alerts (smurfing, burner phone rotations, layering).\n\n---\n\n### Architecture & Security Flow\n\n```\n                      ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                      │    Frontend Client (React/Vite)        │\n                      └───────────────────┬────────────────────┘\n                                          │ HTTP GET + X-Auth-Token\n                                          ▼\n                      ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                      │            CORS Middleware             │\n                      │  Validates Origin, Headers, & Methods  │\n                      └───────────────────┬────────────────────┘\n                                          │\n                                          ▼\n                      ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                      │   RBAC Dependency (require_investigator│\n                      │   - 401 if token missing or invalid    │\n                      │   - 403 if role != 'investigator'      │\n                      └───────────────────┬────────────────────┘\n                                          │ Authenticated Principal\n                     ┌────────────────────┴────────────────────┐\n                     │                                         │\n                     ▼                                         ▼\n       ┌───────────────────────────┐             ┌───────────────────────────┐\n       │   GET /api/network        │             │   GET /api/anomalies      │\n       │   - Injects Neo4j Session │             │   - Runs Anomaly Detector │\n       │   - Cypher: MATCH (n)...  │             │   - Flags Structuring &   │\n       │   - Formats Cytoscape JSON│             │     Burner Rotations      │\n       └───────────────────────────┘             └───────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Complete Backend Application: `main.py`\n\n```python\n# =====================================================================\n# requirements.txt\n# =====================================================================\n# fastapi>=0.110.0\n# uvicorn[standard]>=0.28.0\n# neo4j>=5.18.0\n# pydantic>=2.6.0\n# =====================================================================\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport logging\nimport os\nfrom typing import Any, Generator\n\nfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, Header, HTTPException, status\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\ntry:\n    from neo4j import GraphDatabase, Driver, Session\n    from neo4j.exceptions import ServiceUnavailable, AuthError\n    HAS_NEO4J_DRIVER = True\nexcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover\n    GraphDatabase = None\n    Driver = None\n    Session = None\n    HAS_NEO4J_DRIVER = False\n\n# Setup structured logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(name)s: %(message)s\")\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"law_enforcement_intel_api\")\n\n# =====================================================================\n# Configuration & Environment Variables\n# =====================================================================\n\nNEO4J_URI: str = os.getenv(\"NEO4J_URI\", \"bolt://localhost:7687\")\nNEO4J_USER: str = os.getenv(\"NEO4J_USER\", \"neo4j\")\nNEO4J_PASSWORD: str = os.getenv(\"NEO4J_PASSWORD\", \"password123\")\n\n# Global Neo4j Driver instance pool\n_neo4j_driver: Driver | None = None\n\n\ndef get_driver() -> Driver | None:\n    \"\"\"Initialize or return the global Neo4j driver connection pool.\"\"\"\n    global _neo4j_driver\n    if _neo4j_driver is None and HAS_NEO4J_DRIVER and GraphDatabase is not None:\n        try:\n            _neo4j_driver = GraphDatabase.driver(\n                NEO4J_URI,\n                auth=(NEO4J_USER, NEO4J_PASSWORD),\n                max_connection_lifetime=3600,\n            )\n            logger.info(\"Neo4j driver initialized for URI: %s\", NEO4J_URI)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            logger.warning(\"Failed to initialize Neo4j driver: %s\", exc)\n            _neo4j_driver = None\n    return _neo4j_driver\n\n\ndef close_driver() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Cleanly dispose of the Neo4j connection pool on application shutdown.\"\"\"\n    global _neo4j_driver\n    if _neo4j_driver is not None:\n        try:\n            _neo4j_driver.close()\n            logger.info(\"Neo4j driver connection pool closed.\")\n        except Exception as exc:\n            logger.error(\"Error closing Neo4j driver: %s\", exc)\n        finally:\n            _neo4j_driver = None\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# Realistic Intelligence Fallback Data\n# (Ensures immediate usability when Neo4j is offline or empty)\n# =====================================================================\n\nFALLBACK_CYTOSCAPE_ELEMENTS: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n    # Person Nodes\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"p1\", \"label\": \"Viktor 'The Ghost' Vance\", \"type\": \"person\", \"role\": \"Syndicate Leader\", \"risk\": \"CRITICAL\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"p2\", \"label\": \"Elena Rostova\", \"type\": \"person\", \"role\": \"Logistics Coordinator\", \"risk\": \"HIGH\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"p3\", \"label\": \"Dmitri Volkov\", \"type\": \"person\", \"role\": \"Operations Enforcer\", \"risk\": \"CRITICAL\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"p4\", \"label\": \"Marcus Vance\", \"type\": \"person\", \"role\": \"Corporate Front Director\", \"risk\": \"MEDIUM\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"p5\", \"label\": \"Sarah Chen\", \"type\": \"person\", \"role\": \"Financial Mule\", \"risk\": \"MEDIUM\"}},\n    # Phone Nodes\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"ph1\", \"label\": \"+1 (555) 019-4821 [Burner Alpha]\", \"type\": \"phone\", \"carrier\": \"T-Cell PPD\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"ph2\", \"label\": \"+1 (555) 014-9982 [Burner Beta]\", \"type\": \"phone\", \"carrier\": \"Metro SIM\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"ph3\", \"label\": \"+1 (555) 017-3310 [VoIP Trunk]\", \"type\": \"phone\", \"carrier\": \"SignalMesh Global\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"ph4\", \"label\": \"+1 (555) 012-7804 [Encrypted Sat]\", \"type\": \"phone\", \"carrier\": \"Thuraya Sat\"}},\n    # Account Nodes\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"acc1\", \"label\": \"SWIFT // CH-9804-CY [Cayman Trust]\", \"type\": \"account\", \"balance\": \"$2,450,000\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"acc2\", \"label\": \"USDT // 0x7f29...a81e [Tether Mule]\", \"type\": \"account\", \"balance\": \"$680,000 USDT\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"acc3\", \"label\": \"IBAN // LU-1189-99 [Apex Shell Corp]\", \"type\": \"account\", \"balance\": \"$1,120,000\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"acc4\", \"label\": \"ACH // US-Chase-4891 [Logistics Front]\", \"type\": \"account\", \"balance\": \"$84,500\"}},\n    # Directed Edges\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e1\", \"source\": \"p1\", \"target\": \"ph1\", \"label\": \"OPERATES\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e2\", \"source\": \"p2\", \"target\": \"ph2\", \"label\": \"OPERATES\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e3\", \"source\": \"p3\", \"target\": \"ph3\", \"label\": \"OPERATES\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e4\", \"source\": \"ph1\", \"target\": \"ph2\", \"label\": \"14 CALLS (42m)\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e5\", \"source\": \"ph2\", \"target\": \"ph3\", \"label\": \"BURST SMS\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e6\", \"source\": \"p1\", \"target\": \"ph4\", \"label\": \"SAT BRIDGE\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e7\", \"source\": \"p1\", \"target\": \"p2\", \"label\": \"DIRECTS\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e8\", \"source\": \"p2\", \"target\": \"p3\", \"label\": \"COORDINATES\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e9\", \"source\": \"p1\", \"target\": \"acc1\", \"label\": \"BENEFICIARY\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e10\", \"source\": \"acc1\", \"target\": \"acc2\", \"label\": \"WIRE $450,000\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e11\", \"source\": \"acc2\", \"target\": \"acc3\", \"label\": \"MIXER BRIDGE\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e12\", \"source\": \"p4\", \"target\": \"acc3\", \"label\": \"SIGNATORY\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e13\", \"source\": \"acc3\", \"target\": \"acc4\", \"label\": \"PAYROLL DISBURSE\"}},\n    {\"data\": {\"id\": \"e14\", \"source\": \"p5\", \"target\": \"acc4\", \"label\": \"SMURF WITHDRAWAL\"}},\n]\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# Application Lifespan Context Manager\n# =====================================================================\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    \"\"\"Manages startup connectivity verification and clean shutdown.\"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Starting Law Enforcement Intelligence Platform API...\")\n    driver = get_driver()\n    if driver is not None:\n        try:\n            driver.verify_connectivity()\n            logger.info(\"Neo4j database connection established.\")\n        except Exception as exc:\n            logger.warning(\"Neo4j database offline (%s). Using high-fidelity intelligence fallback.\", exc)\n    else:\n        logger.info(\"Neo4j driver offline. Automated fallback engine enabled.\")\n\n    yield\n\n    logger.info(\"Shutting down API and closing connection pools...\")\n    close_driver()\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# FastAPI App Initialization & CORS Middleware\n# =====================================================================\n\napp = FastAPI(\n    title=\"Law Enforcement Intelligence Platform API\",\n    description=\"Backend service providing criminal network topology and automated anomaly analytics.\",\n    version=\"2.0.0\",\n    lifespan=lifespan,\n)\n\n# Enable CORS for frontend applications (e.g. Vite dev servers)\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=[\n        \"http://localhost:5173\",\n        \"http://localhost:3000\",\n        \"http://127.0.0.1:5173\",\n        \"http://127.0.0.1:3000\",\n        \"*\",  # Permissive for local intelligence testing\n    ],\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\", \"PUT\", \"DELETE\", \"OPTIONS\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# Database Dependency: Neo4j Session Lifecycle\n# =====================================================================\n\ndef get_neo4j_session() -> Generator[Session | None, None, None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    FastAPI dependency yielding a Neo4j database session.\n    Guarantees session closure after route execution completes.\n    Yields None if the database is unreachable, enabling route fallback.\n    \"\"\"\n    driver = get_driver()\n    if driver is None:\n        yield None\n        return\n\n    session = None\n    try:\n        session = driver.session()\n        yield session\n    except (ServiceUnavailable, AuthError) as exc:\n        logger.warning(\"Neo4j service error when opening session: %s\", exc)\n        yield None\n    finally:\n        if session is not None:\n            try:\n                session.close()\n            except Exception as exc:\n                logger.error(\"Failed to close Neo4j session: %s\", exc)\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & Authentication\n# =====================================================================\n\n# Simulated identity directory mapping bearer tokens to law enforcement personnel\nLEO_PERSONNEL: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {\n    \"token-investigator-01\": {\n        \"name\": \"Det. Sarah Miller\",\n        \"role\": \"investigator\",\n        \"unit\": \"Major Narcotics Task Force\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-7402\",\n    },\n    \"token-investigator-02\": {\n        \"name\": \"Special Agent Marcus Vance\",\n        \"role\": \"investigator\",\n        \"unit\": \"Organized Crime Strike Force\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-3319\",\n    },\n    \"demo-investigator\": {\n        \"name\": \"Det. Alex Cross\",\n        \"role\": \"investigator\",\n        \"unit\": \"Special Investigations Division\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-8008\",\n    },\n    \"token-analyst-01\": {\n        \"name\": \"David Park\",\n        \"role\": \"analyst\",\n        \"unit\": \"Financial Intelligence Unit\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-9082\",\n    },\n    \"token-viewer-01\": {\n        \"name\": \"Officer James Cole\",\n        \"role\": \"viewer\",\n        \"unit\": \"Patrol Division\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-5510\",\n    },\n}\n\n\nclass UserPrincipal(BaseModel):\n    name: str\n    role: str\n    unit: str\n    badge: str\n    token: str\n\n\ndef current_user(x_auth_token: str | None = Header(None, alias=\"X-Auth-Token\")) -> UserPrincipal:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates the X-Auth-Token header against authorized law enforcement personnel.\n    Raises HTTP 401 Unauthorized if the token is missing, expired, or invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not x_auth_token:\n        logger.warning(\"Access attempted without X-Auth-Token header.\")\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail=\"Authentication failed: missing X-Auth-Token header.\",\n            headers={\"WWW-Authenticate\": \"X-Auth-Token\"},\n        )\n\n    if x_auth_token not in LEO_PERSONNEL:\n        logger.warning(\"Unauthorized access attempt with invalid token: %s\", x_auth_token)\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail=\"Authentication failed: invalid or unrecognized authorization token.\",\n            headers={\"WWW-Authenticate\": \"X-Auth-Token\"},\n        )\n\n    user_data = LEO_PERSONNEL[x_auth_token]\n    return UserPrincipal(\n        name=user_data[\"name\"],\n        role=user_data[\"role\"],\n        unit=user_data[\"unit\"],\n        badge=user_data[\"badge\"],\n        token=x_auth_token,\n    )\n\n\ndef require_investigator(principal: UserPrincipal = Depends(current_user)) -> UserPrincipal:\n    \"\"\"\n    Enforces Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).\n    Restricts access strictly to users possessing the 'investigator' role.\n    Raises HTTP 403 Forbidden if user clearance is insufficient.\n    \"\"\"\n    if principal.role.lower() != \"investigator\":\n        logger.warning(\n            \"Access Denied: User %s (Badge: %s, Role: '%s') attempted to access investigator endpoint.\",\n            principal.name,\n            principal.badge,\n            principal.role,\n        )\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail=f\"Access denied: role '{principal.role}' does not possess 'investigator' clearance.\",\n        )\n    return principal\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# Response Schemas (OpenAPI Documentation)\n# =====================================================================\n\nclass CytoscapeElement(BaseModel):\n    data: dict[str, Any] = Field(..., description=\"Cytoscape element data payload\")\n\n\nclass NetworkGraphResponse(BaseModel):\n    elements: list[CytoscapeElement]\n    total_nodes: int\n    total_edges: int\n    source: str\n\n\nclass AnomalyRecord(BaseModel):\n    type: str = Field(..., description=\"Classification category of the suspicious behavior\")\n    severity: str = Field(..., description=\"Severity level: low, medium, high, or critical\")\n    entities: list[str] = Field(..., description=\"Entity identifiers involved in the anomaly\")\n    description: str | None = Field(None, description=\"Detailed intelligence assessment\")\n    confidence: float | None = Field(None, description=\"Detection confidence score (0.0 to 1.0)\")\n    timestamp: str | None = Field(None, description=\"ISO-8601 detection timestamp\")\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# Route Endpoints\n# =====================================================================\n\n@app.get(\"/api/health\", tags=[\"System\"])\ndef health_check():\n    \"\"\"Returns database connectivity and service status.\"\"\"\n    driver = get_driver()\n    neo4j_online = False\n    if driver:\n        try:\n            driver.verify_connectivity()\n            neo4j_online = True\n        except Exception:\n            neo4j_online = False\n\n    return {\n        \"status\": \"online\",\n        \"neo4j_connected\": neo4j_online,\n        \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n    }\n\n\n@app.get(\n    \"/api/network\",\n    response_model=NetworkGraphResponse,\n    tags=[\"Intelligence Graph\"],\n    summary=\"Retrieve full criminal network formatted for Cytoscape.js\",\n)\ndef get_network_graph(\n    session: Session | None = Depends(get_neo4j_session),\n    investigator: UserPrincipal = Depends(require_investigator),\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Executes a Cypher query to retrieve all nodes and directed relationships.\n    Formats records into an array of Cytoscape.js elements where each element\n    has a 'data' dictionary containing `id`, `source`, `target`, and `label`.\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Exporting network graph for investigator: %s (%s)\", investigator.name, investigator.badge)\n\n    elements: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    nodes_seen: set[str] = set()\n\n    # Cypher query to fetch all nodes and their directed relationships\n    cypher_query = \"\"\"\n    MATCH (n)\n    OPTIONAL MATCH (n)-[r]->(m)\n    RETURN n, r, m\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if session is not None:\n        try:\n            result = session.run(cypher_query)\n            for record in result:\n                n = record.get(\"n\")\n                r = record.get(\"r\")\n                m = record.get(\"m\")\n\n                # Extract and format nodes\n                for node in (n, m):\n                    if node is not None:\n                        node_id = str(getattr(node, \"element_id\", getattr(node, \"id\", None)))\n                        if node_id not in nodes_seen:\n                            nodes_seen.add(node_id)\n                            labels = list(node.labels) if hasattr(node, \"labels\") else []\n                            primary_label = labels[0] if labels else \"Entity\"\n                            props = dict(node)\n\n                            display_label = props.get(\"label\") or props.get(\"name\") or f\"{primary_label} [{node_id}]\"\n                            node_type = props.get(\"type\") or primary_label.lower()\n\n                            element_data = {\n                                \"id\": node_id,\n                                \"label\": str(display_label),\n                                \"type\": str(node_type),\n                                **props,\n                            }\n                            elements.append({\"data\": element_data})\n\n                # Extract and format directed relationship (edge)\n                if r is not None:\n                    edge_id = str(getattr(r, \"element_id\", getattr(r, \"id\", None)))\n                    start_node = getattr(r, \"start_node\", None)\n                    end_node = getattr(r, \"end_node\", None)\n\n                    start_id = (\n                        str(getattr(start_node, \"element_id\", getattr(start_node, \"id\", None)))\n                        if start_node\n                        else str(getattr(n, \"element_id\", getattr(n, \"id\", \"\")))\n                    )\n                    end_id = (\n                        str(getattr(end_node, \"element_id\", getattr(end_node, \"id\", None)))\n                        if end_node\n                        else str(getattr(m, \"element_id\", getattr(m, \"id\", \"\")))\n                    )\n\n                    edge_props = dict(r)\n                    rel_type = getattr(r, \"type\", \"ASSOCIATED_WITH\")\n                    display_label = edge_props.get(\"label\") or rel_type\n\n                    edge_data = {\n                        \"id\": edge_id,\n                        \"source\": start_id,\n                        \"target\": end_id,\n                        \"label\": str(display_label),\n                        **edge_props,\n                    }\n                    elements.append({\"data\": edge_data})\n\n            if elements:\n                node_count = len(nodes_seen)\n                edge_count = len(elements) - node_count\n                return NetworkGraphResponse(\n                    elements=[CytoscapeElement(data=el[\"data\"]) for el in elements],\n                    total_nodes=node_count,\n                    total_edges=edge_count,\n                    source=\"neo4j_database\",\n                )\n\n        except Exception as exc:\n            logger.warning(\"Failed querying live Neo4j database (%s). Serving simulated network.\", exc)\n\n    # Fallback response if Neo4j is offline or empty\n    logger.info(\"Serving simulated intelligence network elements.\")\n    total_nodes = len([el for el in FALLBACK_CYTOSCAPE_ELEMENTS if \"source\" not in el[\"data\"]])\n    total_edges = len([el for el in FALLBACK_CYTOSCAPE_ELEMENTS if \"source\" in el[\"data\"]])\n\n    return NetworkGraphResponse(\n        elements=[CytoscapeElement(data=el[\"data\"]) for el in FALLBACK_CYTOSCAPE_ELEMENTS],\n        total_nodes=total_nodes,\n        total_edges=total_edges,\n        source=\"simulated_intelligence_fallback\",\n    )\n\n\n@app.get(\n    \"/api/anomalies\",\n    response_model=list[AnomalyRecord],\n    tags=[\"Anomaly Detection\"],\n    summary=\"Run intelligence anomaly detector over graph entities\",\n)\ndef get_anomalies(\n    investigator: UserPrincipal = Depends(require_investigator),\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Simulates automated graph anomaly detection algorithms (smurfing,\n    burner phone rotations, high-velocity layering, command-and-control bypass).\n    Returns flagged intelligence anomalies strictly to authorized investigators.\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.info(\n        \"Automated anomaly scan executed by investigator %s (Badge: %s)\",\n        investigator.name,\n        investigator.badge,\n    )\n\n    # Flagged activity patterns matching the prompt's required schema\n    flagged_activities: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n        {\n            \"type\": \"structuring\",\n            \"severity\": \"high\",\n            \"entities\": [\"acc1\", \"acc2\", \"p5\"],\n            \"description\": \"Repetitive sub-$10,000 cash deposits funneled through mule to unhosted Tether mixer.\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.94,\n            \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        },\n        {\n            \"type\": \"burner_cycling\",\n            \"severity\": \"critical\",\n            \"entities\": [\"ph1\", \"ph2\"],\n            \"description\": \"14 burst calls within 40 minutes across ephemeral SIM cards followed by handset power-down.\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.98,\n            \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        },\n        {\n            \"type\": \"hierarchy_bypass\",\n            \"severity\": \"high\",\n            \"entities\": [\"p1\", \"p3\", \"ph4\"],\n            \"description\": \"Direct communication detected between operational enforcer and Tier-1 cartel principal.\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.89,\n            \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        },\n        {\n            \"type\": \"rapid_layering\",\n            \"severity\": \"medium\",\n            \"entities\": [\"acc2\", \"acc3\", \"acc4\"],\n            \"description\": \"High-velocity capital transfer across multiple offshore shell accounts within 180 seconds.\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.82,\n            \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n        },\n    ]\n\n    return [AnomalyRecord(**item) for item in flagged_activities]\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import uvicorn\n    uvicorn.run(\"main:app\", host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000, reload=True)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Verification and Testing Guide\n\n#### 1. Start the Server\n```bash\nuvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload\n```\n\n#### 2. Test Authorization & RBAC Enforcement\n\n| Scenario | Request | Expected Status | Result |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **Missing Header** | `curl -i http://localhost:8000/api/network` | `401 Unauthorized` | Rejects unauthenticated traffic |\n| **Invalid Token** | `curl -i -H \"X-Auth-Token: invalid-token\" http://localhost:8000/api/network` | `401 Unauthorized` | Rejects unrecognized credentials |\n| **N